  "result": "That decision is made in `src/hooks/shortcut-match.ts`.\n\n- **`matchesShortcut(keys, event, platform)`** first reads the shortcut's parts (for example `[\"mod\", \"k\"]`) using `parseShortcut`. It then checks that the pressed key and the Ctrl, Meta, Alt and Shift states all match the shortcut exactly.\n- **`prefersMetaKey(platform)`** decides what \"mod\" means. If the platform string matches `mac`, `iphone`, `ipad` or `ipod`, \"mod\" means Command (Meta). On anything else it means Control.\n\n`src/hooks/use-keyboard-shortcut.ts` is the hook that listens for key presses. Its only part in this is reading `navigator.platform` and passing it to `matchesShortcut`, so the matching itself isn't done there.\n\nANSWER: src/hooks/shortcut-match.ts",
